&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/incubator-zeppelin/pull/519&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/incubator-zeppelin/pull/519&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-491&quot; title=&quot;Fixed height to container when result type is text&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;ZEPPELIN-491&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;ZEPPELIN-491&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;: Giving fixed height to container when result type is text&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    In current behaviour we have a fixed height for result container that contains either graph or table, but if type is text then the container expands to infinitely.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    When type is text; then this is mostly logs, so we can have scroll around it and have fixed height for this container.&lt;/p&gt;

